/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/methods.k-9-  // method-call routing + arg-eval live in call.k; this module owns applyMethod.
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/methods.k-10-  syntax Val ::= applyMethod(Val, String, Vals) [function]
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/methods.k-11-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/methods.k-12-  // ==== string predicates (Python semantics) =================================
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/methods.k:13:  rule applyMethod(str(CS:IntSeq), "isupper", .Vals) => hasUpper(CS) andBool notBool hasLower(CS)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/methods.k:14:  rule applyMethod(str(CS:IntSeq), "islower", .Vals) => hasLower(CS) andBool notBool hasUpper(CS)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/methods.k:15:  rule applyMethod(str(CS:IntSeq), "isalpha", .Vals) => notBool (CS ==K .IntSeq) andBool allAlpha(CS)
